notes: V037 is an owner-requested new patch after V036; R2 adds single-window adaptive payload control. It keeps the V036 persistent ATL1 length-prefixed TCP JPEG wire format and multi-ESP architecture, but adds adaptive JPEG pressure control on the ESP to reduce frame size when measured send time, large JPEGs, or transport failures show that the link cannot sustain the configured image load. New camera profiles default to QVGA / JPEG quality 24 / 15 FPS while existing saved profiles remain unchanged. The ESP targets roughly 5 KB JPEG payloads, locally skips oversized captures while compression can increase, learns a lower target from partial sends, and exposes configured/effective quality, target bytes, local-drop/window-learn counts, adjustment count and send-time EWMA. PC Studio identifies V037 as current while accepting V036 binary-TCP camera nodes during migration. V024 / 0_2_4 remains the owner-confirmed passed baseline until explicit owner acceptance changes it. Physical/public-road signal control remains disabled.
